H2001.def:
A man living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Esther 3:1; 
son of: Hammedatha (H4099); married to Zeresh (H2238); 
father of: Parshandatha (H6577), Dalphon (H1813), Aspatha (H0630), Poratha (H6334), Adalia (H0118), Aridatha (H0743), Parmashta (H6534), Arisai (H0747), Aridai (H0742), Vaizatha (H2055) 
§ Haman = "magnificent"
chief minister of Ahasuerus, enemy of Mordecai and the Jews, who plotted to kill the Jews but, being foiled by Esther, was hanged, with his family, on the gallows he had made for Mordecai

H2037.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 4:8; 
son of: Koz (H6976); 
brother of: Anub (H6036) and Zobebah (H6637); 
father of: Aharhel (H0316) 
§ Harum = "exalted"
a man of Judah, father of Aharhel

H2039G.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 11:26; 
son of: Terah (H8646); 
brother of: Abraham (H0085), Nahor (H5152H) and Sarah (H8283); 
father of: Lot (H3876), Milcah (H4435) and Iscah (H3252)
§ Haran = "mountaineer"
1) youngest son of Terah, brother of Abraham, father of Lot, Milcah, and Iscah; born and died in Ur of the Chaldees
2) a Gershonite Levite in the time of David, one of the family of Shimei
3) a son of Caleb by the concubine Ephah
4) name of the place to which Abraham migrated from Ur of the Chaldees and where the descendants of his brother Nahor established themselves; probably located in Mesopotamia, in Padanaram, the cultivated district at the foot of the hills between the Khabour and the Euphrates below Mount Masius

H2044.def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 23:32; 
also called Hashem at 1 Chroniques 11:34;
Another name of ya.shen (יָשֵׁן "Jashen" H3464) 
§ Hashem = "fat"
a Gizonite, father of some sons who were members of David's mighty warriors

H2055.def:
A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Esther 9:9; 
son of: Haman (H2001); 
brother of: Parshandatha (H6577), Dalphon (H1813), Aspatha (H0630), Poratha (H6334), Adalia (H0118), Aridatha (H0743), Parmashta (H6534), Arisai (H0747) and Aridai (H0742) 
§ Vajezatha = "strong as the wind"
one of the 10 sons of Haman who were hanged with their father

H2059.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Samuel 8:2; 
son of: Samuel (H8050); 
brother of: Abijah (H0029); 
father of: Heman (H1968I); also translated "second" at 1 Chroniques 6:28; 
Another name of yo.el (יוֹאֵל "Joel" H3100G) 
§ Vashni = "strong"
a son of Samuel

H2067G.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Josué 7:1; 
son of: Zerah (H2226I); 
brother of: Ethan (H0387H), Heman (H1968H), Calcol (H3633H) and Dara (H1873); 
father of: Carmi (H3756H); also called Zimri at 1 Chroniques 2:6; 
Also named: zim.ri (זִמְרִי "Zimri" H2174I)
§ Zabdi = "endowment"
1) son of Zerah and grandson of Judah; grandfather of Achan
2) one of the sons of Shimhi, a Benjamite
3) an officer of David, in charge of the produce of the vineyards for the wine-cellars
4) son of Asaph the minstrel; also called 'Zaccur' and 'Zichri'

H2067J.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 9:15; 
son of: Asaph (H0623I); 
father of: Mica (H4316); also called Zabdi at Néhémie 11:17;
Another name of zikh.ri (זִכְרִי "Zichri" H2147K)
§ Zabdi = "endowment"
1) son of Zerah and grandson of Judah; grandfather of Achan
2) one of the sons of Shimhi, a Benjamite
3) an officer of David, in charge of the produce of the vineyards for the wine-cellars
4) son of Asaph the minstrel; also called 'Zaccur' and 'Zichri'

H2071.def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Rois 4:5; 
son of: Nathan (H5416H); 
brother of: Azariah (H5838H) 
§ Zabud = "given"
a priest, son of Nathan, who held the post of 'king's friend' to Solomon

H2074.def:
A man of the tribe of Zebulun living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 30:20; 
son of: Israel (H3478) and Leah (H3812); 
brother of: Reuben (H7205), Simeon (H8095), Levi (H3878), Judah (H3063), Issachar (H3485) and Dinah (H1783); 
half-brother of: Dan (H1835H), Naphtali (H5321), Gad (H1410), Asher (H0836), Joseph (H3130) and Benjamin (H1144); 
father of: Sered (H5624), Elon (H0356H) and Jahleel (H3177) 
§ Zebulun = "exalted"
1) the 10th of the sons of Jacob, 6th and last of Leah; progenitor of Zebulun
2) the tribe descended from Zebulun
3) the land allocated to the tribe of Zebulun

H2075.def:
Someone from the tribe of Zebulun living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 30:20; 
son of: Israel (H3478) and Leah (H3812); 
brother of: Reuben (H7205), Simeon (H8095), Levi (H3878), Judah (H3063), Issachar (H3485) and Dinah (H1783); 
half-brother of: Dan (H1835H), Naphtali (H5321), Gad (H1410), Asher (H0836), Joseph (H3130) and Benjamin (H1144); 
father of: Sered (H5624), Elon (H0356H) and Jahleel (H3177)
Group of ze.vu.lun (זְבוּלֻן "Zebulun" H2074) 
§ Zebulonite , of Zebulun
a descendant of Zebulun and member of the tribe of Zebulun

H2080.def:
A woman living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2 Rois 23:36; 
daughter of: Pedaiah (H6305); married to Josiah (H2977); 
mother of: Jehoiakim (H3079) 
§ Zebudah = "given"
wife of Josiah and mother of Jehoiakim, both kings of Judah

H2093.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2 Chroniques 11:19; 
son of: Rehoboam (H7346) and Mahalath (H4258H); 
brother of: Jeush (H3266K) and Shemariah (H8114H); 
half-brother of: Abijah (H0029I), Attai (H6262I), Ziza (H2124H) and Shelomith (H8019G) 
§ Zaham = "loathing"
the son of Rehoboam by Mahalath, David's granddaughter
